{#
    The in-app notification indicator (FR-093, G-33).

    **The count is in the link's text, not only in a coloured dot.** A badge that conveys "you
    have three" by being red and round conveys nothing to a screen reader and nothing to a reader
    who cannot distinguish it from decoration (NFR-094, WCAG 1.4.1). So the number is written out,
    the visible badge is `aria-hidden`, and the accessible name says what the number counts.

    Two different things are counted, because they are two different facts: unread messages, and
    purchases actually waiting on this parent. A parent who has read every email still has
    decisions to make, and an indicator that conflated them would go quiet while three children
    waited.

    Renders as a plain link when there is nothing outstanding — never disappears, so the inbox
    stays reachable from every page rather than only from the pages that happen to have news.
#}
{% set unread = unread_notification_count() %}
{% set pending = is_granted('ACCOUNT_MANAGE_PAYMENT_METHODS') ? pending_approval_count() : 0 %}

<a href="{{ path('notifications_index') }}">
    Notifications
    {% if unread > 0 %}
        <span class="badge" aria-hidden="true">{{ unread }}</span>
        <span class="visually-hidden">
            — {{ unread }} unread{% if pending > 0 %}, {{ pending }} purchase{{ pending == 1 ? '' : 's' }} waiting for your approval{% endif %}
        </span>
    {% elseif pending > 0 %}
        <span class="badge" aria-hidden="true">{{ pending }}</span>
        <span class="visually-hidden">— {{ pending }} purchase{{ pending == 1 ? '' : 's' }} waiting for your approval</span>
    {% endif %}
</a>
